# .env.example — Environment variables for magic-agents
#
# Copy this file to .env.test for local testing, or set real values in your shell.
# Tests that require live API keys will skip if placeholders are detected.
#
# NEVER commit real API keys to this file or any test file.

# ─── LLM Provider Keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OpenAI API key (required for LLM nodes with engine="openai")
# Tests skip if this is empty or looks like a placeholder
OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key-here

# ─── Optional External Services ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# Serper API key (optional, used for search/fetch nodes)
# Tests skip if this is empty or placeholder
SERPER_API_KEY=your-serper-api-key-here

# Jina API key (optional, used for embedding/search)
JINA_API_KEY=your-jina-api-key-here

# ─── Test Environment Notes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# For local testing:
#   1. Copy this file to .env.test: cp .env.example .env.test
#   2. Replace placeholders with real keys in .env.test
#   3. OR set real keys in your shell environment (takes priority)
#
# For CI environments:
#   - Set real keys directly in CI secrets/environment
#   - .env.test is a fallback only (loaded by test/conftest.py)
#
# Test behavior when keys are missing/placeholder:
#   - Tests that require live external APIs will skip honestly
#   - Tests that can run with mocked data will proceed
#   - No hardcoding of secrets in test files
